# netsurf: a structural match restyles only the matching siblings when that is enough (patch 405)
# Generated 2026-11-08
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 404)
#
# Patch 404 answered a structural match on a child-list change by
# rebuilding the parent's subtree; on the 21 sites that converted almost
# nothing: the matches are mostly on <body> (youtube appends <iframe>s
# there), whose subtree holds frames and controls, which the container
# rebuild declines ("holds controls or frames" 8 of 10 in r115). And only
# one child flips there: the old last child, when something is appended
# after it.
#
#  - html_rl_struct_scan: each structural compound records sib_after --
#    a sibling combinator (+ ~) follows it (for one inside :not()/:is()/...,
#    the OUTER compound, past the group; nested deeper, unknown: set): then
#    a flip restyles another element than the matching one.
#  - html_rl_block_struct_risk: optional hits/nhits/narrow -- every child
#    a structural rule matches is collected (referenced, at most 8);
#    narrow when each matching compound is bounded and has no sibling
#    combinator after it, no sheet overflowed, nothing ran out.
#  - html_rl_block_change: narrow -> the blocks are placed as usual and
#    the matching siblings restyled alone at the success exits
#    (html_rl_struct_hits_finish), or in place of patch 378's no-op; each
#    by the container rebuild of 372/376 (its guards unchanged). A matching
#    child with no box, or not a block-level box of the parent, declines
#    into the full rebuild. Not narrow -> 404's parent-subtree route. The
#    references are released on every exit.
# Logged "LIFE rebuild local: structural change: N matching sibling(s)
# restyled alone in N us (M so far)".
#
# Measured: a 500-row feed with .row:last-child, 10 appends -- 404's parent
# subtree 12.7 ms per append (median), this 1.66 ms. On the 21 scorecard
# sites it converts nothing: youtube's matches are unbounded bare
# :last-child compounds on the previous <iframe> (a frame's box is not
# rebuilt), so the census needs an in-place restyle there.
#
